@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Navigating Azure DevOps UI";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="text-center lead">Once your Azure DevOps organization is set up, it's essential to understand its user interface (UI) to manage projects effectively. The Azure DevOps UI provides a seamless experience for teams to collaborate on code, track work, and automate workflows.</p>
    <hr />

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Overview of Azure DevOps UI</h2>
        <p>The Azure DevOps UI consists of several key sections, each serving a specific purpose:</p>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center">
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h4>1. Navigation Bar</h4>
            <p>The top navigation bar provides access to different services like Boards, Repos, Pipelines, Test Plans, and Artifacts. Users can switch between projects and organizations from here.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/azure-devops-navigation.png" alt="Azure DevOps Navigation Bar" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Azure DevOps Navigation Bar</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center mt-4">
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/azure-devops-project-dashboard.png" alt="Azure DevOps Project Dashboard" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Azure DevOps Project Dashboard</small></p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h4>2. Project Dashboard</h4>
            <p>Displays an overview of active projects, work items, repositories, and pipelines. It helps users quickly access recent activities and ongoing work.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center mt-4">
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h4>3. Boards</h4>
            <p>Azure Boards is used for project management, offering tools like Kanban boards, Scrum boards, backlogs, and sprint planning.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/azure-boards-example.png" alt="Azure Boards" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Managing tasks with Azure Boards</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center mt-4">
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/azure-repos-ui.png" alt="Azure Repos UI" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Version control with Azure Repos</small></p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h4>4. Repos</h4>
            <p>Azure Repos provides Git-based source control with features like pull requests, branch policies, and code reviews.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center mt-4">
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h4>5. Pipelines</h4>
            <p>Azure Pipelines allows you to automate builds, testing, and deployments through CI/CD workflows.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/azure-pipelines-overview.png" alt="Azure Pipelines UI" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Azure Pipelines for CI/CD automation</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center mt-4">
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/azure-test-plans.png" alt="Azure Test Plans UI" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Test management with Azure Test Plans</small></p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h4>6. Test Plans</h4>
            <p>Azure Test Plans allows teams to execute manual and automated tests to ensure software quality.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center mt-4">
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h4>7. Artifacts</h4>
            <p>Azure Artifacts is a package management system that helps teams share and manage dependencies securely.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/azure-artifacts.png" alt="Azure Artifacts UI" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Managing dependencies with Azure Artifacts</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
            Understanding the Azure DevOps UI is crucial for managing projects effectively. With an intuitive dashboard, navigation bar, and integrated tools, teams can seamlessly collaborate, track progress, and automate workflows.
        </p>
        <p>
            The next step is to **create and manage projects** within Azure DevOps.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex justify-content-between mt-4">
        <a href="@Url.Action("SettingUpAnAzureDevOpsOrganization", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">&larr; Previous: Setting up an Azure DevOps Organization</a>
        <a href="@Url.Action("CreatingAndManagingProjects", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">Next: Creating and Managing Projects &rarr;</a>
    </div>
</div>